From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:32:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: present 10-bit XRGB/ARGB2101010 on the
 J604 panel

The T8132 panel's primary plane offers only XRGB8888 and ARGB8888, so a
compositor asked for 10 bits a component (Hyprland bitdepth = 10, the
wide-colour and HDR modes) falls back to 8 bits, although the firmware
takes 10-bit surfaces (below). On a MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) with this
kernel, a runtime Hyprland rule with cm = "dp3" and bitdepth = 10 leaves
the output at XRGB8888 (hyprctl currentFormat).

The firmware takes a 10-bit surface with one change to the 8-bit one: the
pixel format OSType at surface +0x0b is 'l10r' (0x6c313072), CoreVideo's
kCVPixelFormatType_ARGB2101010LEPacked, "little-endian ARGB2101010
full-range", which is DRM's [A|X]RGB2101010 bit for bit. Everything else
stays: 4 bytes a pixel, one linear plane, the stride rule, and the SDR
colour tags (P3-D65 primaries, sRGB transfer). An earlier out-of-tree
version of this change ran the panel at XRGB2101010 3024x1964 at 120 Hz
under Hyprland with no DCP error (2026-11-03); it was left out when the
driver moved onto the in-tree backend.

- dcp-m4-frame.h: DCP_M4_XRGB2101010 and DCP_M4_ARGB2101010, one DRM to
  M4 mapping (dcp_m4_drm_format()) for the atomic check and the present
  path, and the OSType and premultiplied byte (+2, set for the X formats
  as for XRGB8888) from the format.
- plane.c: the primary plane lists XRGB2101010 and ARGB2101010 after the
  8888 formats, so a compositor that asks for nothing new picks as before.
- The idle cache surface takes the depth of the frame on screen, so a
  static 10-bit desktop is not cached at 8 bits (same size, 4 bytes a
  pixel). Whether the firmware fills an 'l10r' cache surface is checked on
  the J604 in the dev-loop boot (debugfs iomfb_m4 idle entries, no
  "idle caching refused").

Not offered: XBGR/ABGR2101010 and the 1010102 orders (no firmware format
with that component order), the extended-range 'w30r' and FP16 (not
qualified on 26.6.2). Upper (cursor) surfaces and the external outputs
stay 8888. The 8888 surface is byte for byte as before (KUnit
apple-dcp-m4-frame, against the previous encoder).

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Makefile            |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame-test.c | 140 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame.h      |  80 ++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c          |  12 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4_present.h  |   7 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/plane.c             |   2 +
 6 files changed, 230 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-frame-test.c

